2 specialisations / talent trees: Frost Mage & Electric Mage

Frost Mage overview:
- lots of area control
- slow enemies with frost/ice spells
- try to avoid direct contact with enemies -- keep them at a distance as much as possible
- able to focus on & control multiple enemies at once

Electric Mage overview:
- high burst damage with electric spells
- can chain lightning to hit multiple enemies
- able to stun enemies with electric shocks
- try to avoid direct contact with enemies -- keep them at a distance as much as possible
- mainly focus on single target damage, but a few ways to hit multiple enemeies at once


Frost Mage basic abilities:
- Frost Bolt: A ranged spell that deals frost damage and slows the target.
- Frost Breath: area of effect spell that does not much damage but slows all enemies in the effected area.
- Icy Veins: reduce damage taken
- As Light As Snow: place down a small platform that only Frost Mages can walk on (disappears after 5s after walked on)



Electric Mage basic abilities:
- Lightning Bolt: A ranged spell that deals electric damage to a single target.
- Chain Lightning: A spell that jumps between multiple enemies, dealing electric damage to each (reducing in damage with each jump).
- Small Storm: summons a dark cloud in an area that sporadically sends bolts of lightning down from the cloud (hits visible and non-visible enemies alike)
- Tazer: zap an adjacent enemy, stunning them for 2s


Mage basic abilities (shared):
- Fireball: shoot a small fireball that does small damage when it first hits, then more small damage over time
- Teleport: teleport forward a moderate distance